s":"Rod Bolger","x":"Our results this quarter included pre-tax severance costs of $66 million, which brings our full-year severance to approximately $240 million pre-tax.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2017/11/29/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q4-2017-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2017 Q4","e":"ry","d":"2017-11-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"Operating leverage in Canadian Banking was 1.5% in Q4, and for the full year, adjusted operating leverage was 0.9% including the elevated severance costs, or 1.3% if you exclude the severance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2017/11/29/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q4-2017-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2018 Q1","e":"ry","d":"2018-02-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David McKay","x":"Some banks may report in Treasury and pass it on to the business through transfer pricing, so we happened to deal with it in this business as a stand-alone unit.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/02/23/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q1-2018-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2018 Q1","e":"ry","d":"2018-02-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"We continue to invest in technology and automation as we streamline processes and enhance the client experience.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/02/23/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q1-2018-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2018 Q1","e":"ry","d":"2018-02-23","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Neil McLaughlin","x":"We saw that throughout the entire quarter, and that ended up with origination slightly above Q1 '17, so we are expecting some slowing in the second quarter, but we're maintaining our outlook of mid-single digits, and essentially, the mix of insured to uninsured is about exactly where it's been.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/02/23/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q1-2018-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2018 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2018-05-24","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David I. McKay","x":"The 2% to 3% is -- so, that is an opportunity for us in terms of not expecting to have a severance expense of that size this year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/05/24/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q2-2018-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2018 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2018-05-24","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Robert Sedran","x":"Just to follow up quickly on that operating leverage comment, I remember last year toward the back half, there were some fairly meaningful severance expenses that were affecting some of the year-on-year comps.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/05/24/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q2-2018-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2018 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2018-08-22","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"…is a lot of judgment, and the ways -- the way that certain banks would interpret some of the tariffs and global trade risk as well as the fact that many economists are calling that we're at full employment or below full employment in the US and Canada, with the addition of the cycle being so","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/08/22/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q3-2018-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2018 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2018-08-22","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"David McKay","x":"And when we kind of sat down and think about the impacts of macro drivers on our portfolio, on our credit quality, we talk about more like things like NAFTA, and trade agreements, and auto tariffs, which were still at the time of the cycle.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/08/22/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q3-2018-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2018 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2018-08-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"We had higher than normal severance costs last year, which provided a lift to earnings growth this quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/08/22/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q3-2018-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2018 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2018-08-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"Our expenses were up 6% from a year ago or 8% excluding the severance we took last year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/08/22/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q3-2018-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2018 Q4","e":"ry","d":"2018-11-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"While housing prices remain stretched in key markets, price appreciation stabilized nationally with very modest price increases in Toronto and Vancouver.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/28/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q4-2018-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2018 Q4","e":"ry","d":"2018-11-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Graeme Hepworth","x":"Increase in PCL in securities this quarter relates to writedowns following the restructuring of the Barbados government debt.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/28/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q4-2018-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2018 Q4","e":"ry","d":"2018-11-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Ebrahim Poonawala","x":"I appreciate your comments around deposit betas rightsizing and pricing competition in the U.S. getting harder on deposits.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/28/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q4-2018-earnings-conferenc.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2019 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2019-05-22","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Dave McKay","x":"Trade tariffs are expected to temper GDP growth.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/23/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q2-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2019 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2019-05-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Dave McKay","x":"Our cost structure continues to improve through investments in technology initiatives, which are streamlining processes and creating efficiencies.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/23/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q2-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2019 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2019-05-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Sumit Malhotra","x":"And, certainly, you've avoided taking any of the restructuring charges or one-time factors that some of your peers may have benefited from in the short term.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/23/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q2-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2019 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2019-05-22","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"We maintain our guidance from last quarter and expect City National NIM to be range-bound from year-to-date levels, assuming no rate cuts for the rest of the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/23/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q2-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2019 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2019-08-21","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"We reaffirm our guidance from last quarter and expect lower expense growth in the second half of the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/21/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q3-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2019 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2019-08-21","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Graeme Hepworth","x":"So, each quarter, I would just continue to reiterate the guidance I provided previously.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/21/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q3-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2019 Q4","e":"ry","d":"2019-12-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"But we'll see what happens with the trade discussions and tariffs and future Fed activity.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/12/04/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q4-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2019 Q4","e":"ry","d":"2019-12-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David McKay","x":"We are upgrading our treasury management systems and technology to streamline the onboarding of new clients.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/12/04/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q4-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2019 Q4","e":"ry","d":"2019-12-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Ebrahim Poonawala","x":"And we shouldn't be expecting any bigger actions on expenses like the restructuring you did?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/12/04/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q4-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2020 Q1","e":"ry","d":"2020-02-21","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"David McKay","x":"So you'll see us likely launch a direct-to-consumer bank in the United States sometime at the end of this year, or early next year, really focused on a higher net worth customer, not just similar to some of our competitors in the U.S., what they've done.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/21/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q1-2020-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2020 Q1","e":"ry","d":"2020-02-21","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"David McKay","x":"So as we evolve in the U.S., we shift from a largely commercial cross sold into Wealth to a balance between kind of a high net worth -- ultra high net worth client, we'll move down a little bit down market into super affluent and look at the direct-to-consumer strategy filling in behind there.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/21/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q1-2020-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2020 Q1","e":"ry","d":"2020-02-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"We saw a reduction in headcount through attrition and continue to reduce branch square footage.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/21/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q1-2020-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2020 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2020-05-27","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"David McKay","x":"And we believe our past investments in building unique capabilities such as Borealis AI, Insight Edge and MyAdvisor will significantly differentiate us in the future and enable us to deliver even more value for our clients.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/27/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q2-2020-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2020 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2020-05-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"We would expect to see opportunities for cost savings going forward, assuming client preferences continue to trend toward digital interactions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/27/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q2-2020-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"RY 2020 Q4","e":"ry","d":"2020-12-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"Starting with expenses, which were down 4% year over year or down 2% when excluding the impact of severance and related costs within I&TS last year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/12/02/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q4-2020-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"RY 2020 Q4","e":"ry","d":"2020-12-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"Investor and treasury services net income of $91 million, increased $46 million from a year ago as the prior year included severance and related costs associated repositioning the business.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/12/02/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q4-2020-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"RY 2021 Q1","e":"ry","d":"2021-02-24","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Dave McKay","x":"There's -- there's lending we do direct to consumer through our branches and then the autos -- our auto business.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/24/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q1-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"RY 2021 Q1","e":"ry","d":"2021-02-24","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rod Bolger","x":"This follows on a similar year-over-year decline last quarter after adjusting for severance and related costs associated with the repositioning of I&TS in Q4 '19.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/24/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q1-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"RY 2021 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2021-08-25","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Neil McLaughlin","x":"As we look at, again, the focus on value for money for our customers, we feel there is good value in the RBC direct investing platform in terms of the toolsets we have there, the top tier research, one of the few to provide free streaming quotes.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/25/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q3-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"RY 2021 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2021-08-25","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Dave McKay","x":"It's very straightforward to build a direct-to-consumer deposit bank, but you pay wholesale rates or plus for those deposits that make it very difficult.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/25/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q3-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"RY 2021 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2021-08-25","l":"dtc","r":"management","s":"Dave McKay","x":"And yes, it's something that I could see RBC doing in a direct-to-consumer way.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/25/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q3-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"RY 2021 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2021-08-25","l":"dtc","r":"management","s":"Dave McKay","x":"But a direct-to-consumer with a strategic partner is a very effective way to go to market versus a funding model of direct-to-consumer, which is high-cost savings is always accessible to us.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/25/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q3-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"RY 2021 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2021-08-25","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Dave McKay","x":"So Obviously, price increases are part of this.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/25/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q3-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"RY 2022 Q1","e":"ry","d":"2022-02-24","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Nadine Ahn","x":"And we will continue to invest in efficiency initiatives that streamline and simplify our operations and processes.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/02/24/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q1-2022-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"RY 2022 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2022-08-24","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Graeme Hepworth","x":"As clients at that trigger point and the interest rates continue to increase, it's just the incremental interest cost that's passed through in the immediate, right?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/08/24/royal-bank-of-canada-ry-q3-2022-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"RY 2026 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2026-05-28","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"David McKay","x":"With the leading Canadian franchise as well as the a 10 ranked global business, we are in a great position to support and grow alongside key macro trends, including AI, energy, digital infrastructure and aerospace and defense around the world.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/29/royal-bank-ry-q2-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"RY 2026 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2026-05-28","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"David McKay","x":"In AI and related infrastructure, we advised CPPIB on its U.S. $4.2 billion acquisition of atNorth, a Pan-Nordic data center operator, as well as acted as joint active book runner on Alphabet's $8.5 billion inaugural Maple senior unsecured notes offering, the largest bond offering ever in the…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/29/royal-bank-ry-q2-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"RY 2026 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2026-05-28","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"David McKay","x":"Firstly, tariff-driven uncertainty is having a disproportionate impact on the growth in trade-exposed sectors such as supply chain.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/29/royal-bank-ry-q2-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"RY 2026 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2026-05-28","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"David McKay","x":"So far, weakness in tariff-exposed sectors has not spread to the broader economy, with growth seen in several sectors, including energy and agriculture.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/29/royal-bank-ry-q2-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"RY 2026 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2026-05-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David McKay","x":"We've developed over 200 leading-edge AI models, rethinking how we operate, streamline workflows and delivering more hyper-personalized client experiences by leveraging our proprietary ATOM Foundation model and our increasing data scale within our Lumina platform.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/29/royal-bank-ry-q2-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"RY 2026 Q2","e":"ry","d":"2026-05-28","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Katherine Gibson","x":"We also maintain our guidance of full year all-bank expense growth in the mid-single-digit range, and positive all-bank operating leverage, including higher variable compensation and costs associated with growth-related initiatives and continued investments in our safety and soundness framework.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/29/royal-bank-ry-q2-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"RY 2026 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2026-08-27","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Derek Neldner","x":"I'll maybe take your first question on the AI CapEx cycle.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/31/rbc-ry-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RY 2026 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2026-08-27","l":"ai_spend","r":"analyst","s":"David McKay","x":"Taking a step back to look at the global landscape, market conditions have remained largely constructive, with megatrends continuing to shape critical sectors, including natural resources, power infrastructure, strategic defense, health care and the AI ecosystem.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/31/rbc-ry-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RY 2026 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2026-08-27","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Katherine Gibson","x":"On the trade front, CUSMA moving to an annual review cycle has left tariff exemptions intact for goods and services covered under the pact.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/31/rbc-ry-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RY 2026 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2026-08-27","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Katherine Gibson","x":"Nevertheless, last week, we saw the implementation of new Section 338 tariffs on Canadian exports to the U.S. As these apply to a narrow base of Canadian products, these tariffs alone are not expected to meaningfully change our overall economic forecast.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/31/rbc-ry-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RY 2026 Q3","e":"ry","d":"2026-08-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"John Aiken","x":"And then also in our back office, being able to streamline our processes, think end-to-end, take costs down, increase our service levels.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/31/rbc-ry-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[31,1,9901,0,0,0,7435,1799],[32,1,9603,0,0,0,7137,1813],[33,1,9065,0,0,0,6240,2062],[34,1,10223,0,0,0,6887,2830],[35,1,10823,0,0,0,6510,3796],[37,1,9745,0,0,0,6510,2572],[38,1,9706,0,0,0,7573,1511],[39,1,10453,0,0,0,8458,1575],[40,1,10393,0,0,0,7935,1962],[41,1,11059,0,0,0,9098,1539],[42,1,12631,0,0,0,11060,1185],[43,1,11791,0,0,0,9803,1524],[44,1,11020,0,0,0,9010,1509],[45,1,10555,0,0,0,8271,1882],[46,1,10841,0,0,0,9190,1266],[47,1,13202,0,0,0,10272,2392],[48,1,11850,0,0,0,8854,2499],[49,1,12112,0,0,0,9563,2121],[50,1,11868,0,0,0,9382,2088],[65,1,9633,0,0,0,8278,1158],[66,1,8740,0,0,0,4076,4405]],"cinema":[[31,1,9901,0,0,0,7435,1799],[32,1,9603,0,0,0,7137,1813],[33,1,9065,0,0,0,6240,2062],[34,1,10223,0,0,0,6887,2830],[35,1,10823,0,0,0,6510,3796],[37,1,9745,0,0,0,6510,2572],[38,1,9